ng too attached to the  physical goods themselves because what  happens if you lose them what happens if  they burn up in a fire then you've lost  your love all of a sudden no I don't  think so so I think what we need to let  go of first is the love of the things  and then figure out how do these things  add value and then what is the  appropriate amount for you and not  didn't don't go past the appropriate  amount so  Shelbie makeup perfume candles books  clothing these are all things that  people struggle with right and all  things that I've struggled with  throughout my life as well right but I  think it comes back to we've talked a  lot about boundaries during this and  it's yeah how much do you need to  actually be happy with what you have  because if we're talking things like  makeup if you just buy all this makeup  like if there's a huge makeup culture on  YouTube it's really a problem and if you  paid enough attention to that you'll  think you need every eyeshadow release  that comes out but you have to set  boundaries because realistically you  will never work through all that stuff  if you buy it so aside from like is it  clearing up your space it's like can I  actually use that is this money just  funneling into a product that I'll never  really touch you get value for am I  gonna use it once or twice even though  and then move on from like you didn't  the clothes when you're a teenager  exactly yeah word this once or twice and  now I've moved on I think there is a  fast makeup culture right now on YouTube  for sure well my mother's it looked like  someone was trying to start a makeup  store when when I was going through her  things like she had boxes and bins and  tubs of makeup I think some of us from  the 80s like wow what was going on there  but she it was like yeah all she needed  was the pink Cadillac and she could have  just gone around selling makeup  everything everything would have been  fine  Ryan yes what it what candles candles no  I mean I a